# Signed webhook (Day 5): a request from a system we do not control.
#
# The server computes hmac_sha256(secret, raw_body) and compares it to the
# x-signature header with hmac.compare_digest. A correct signature is accepted
# with 201; a forged one is refused with 401, before the payload is used.
#
# The signature below is pinned to the EXACT body bytes on the request line.
# The body must stay byte-for-byte identical, or the signature will not match.
# The shared secret is "shared-webhook-secret" (in real code it comes from
# configuration, never hard-coded).
#
# To regenerate the signature after changing the body, run:
#   python -c "import hmac,hashlib; print(hmac.new(b'shared-webhook-secret', open('body.txt','rb').read(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest())"
# where body.txt holds the exact bytes you will send.
#
# Start the server first:  poetry run reviews serve

@host = http://127.0.0.1:8000

### Valid signature: the review is accepted with 201 and stored.
# Body: {"product_id": "P9", "rating": 4}
POST {{host}}/v1/webhooks/rating
Content-Type: application/json
x-signature: 07113928ea47145d3439119bfbe59ad3e835950969599dab65f312fb0d1753e3

{"product_id": "P9", "rating": 4}

### Forged signature: the same body with a wrong signature is refused with 401,
### and nothing is stored.
POST {{host}}/v1/webhooks/rating
Content-Type: application/json
x-signature: forged

{"product_id": "P9", "rating": 4}

### Proof: after the valid call above (and only that one), insight counts one review.
GET {{host}}/v1/insight
